seedsync (0.9.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Streamed large path-pair models progressively with bounded worker memory
  * Added bounded performance diagnostics for runtime and model-building work
  * Reduced recursive scan and idle-controller CPU and memory usage
  * Reconciled path-pair scans progressively without transient file removals
  * Fixed no-clobber final moves on Unraid/FUSE and filesystems that reject
    no-replace rename flags

 -- Johan Rosén <johan.rosen.91@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:14:58 +0200

seedsync (0.9.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Added multiple path pairs for independent remote and local libraries,
    including pair-scoped queue, staging, extraction, and validation behavior
  * Added reliable live progress across active, stopped, resumed, and completed
    transfers, with monotonic handoffs and clearer completion status
  * Added trusted-browser sessions and scoped API keys with claim, remember,
    rotate, revoke, same-origin, and first-run access protections
  * Added configurable Generic Webhook and Apprise notifications for download,
    extraction, and successful remote-delete events
  * Added selectable LFTP SFTP/FTPS and rclone SFTP transfer backends while
    isolating credentials from process arguments and diagnostic output
  * Added retained, searchable, severity/time-filtered logs with redaction and
    bounded diagnostic breadcrumbs for transfer investigations
  * Added responsive large-library file views with virtualization, configurable
    pagination, download-time and status sorting, and consistent row states
  * Added a guarded v0.8.6 migration checkpoint with verified private backup,
    user-paced browser handoff, restart recovery, and exact offline restore
  * Hardened path-pair persistence, canonical identity, move completion, and
    deployment-root continuity across restart and configuration changes
  * Improved Docker and Unraid compatibility for numeric UID/GID deployments,
    active-root validation, host-platform Angular builds, and multi-arch images
  * Improved SSE responsiveness, AutoQueue idle behavior, mobile progress
    layout, visible version reporting, and transfer status controls

 -- Johan Rosén <johan.rosen.91@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 18:32:54 +0200

